Package: homelab-svc-hosts
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, perl (>= 5.36), libyaml-libyaml-perl
Recommends: homelab-agent
Description: Internal service-name resolution for the homelab-* fleet
 Seeds a managed block in /etc/hosts mapping stable internal service names
 (api.svc.homelab, pgbouncer.svc.homelab, db.svc.homelab, ...) to their
 VIP/host addresses on the 10.50 service plane, so homelab-* configs can
 reference stable names instead of raw IPs.
 .
 These names are internal-only and always resolve to the internal VIP; they
 never change at cutover (only public FQDNs flip, in authoritative DNS). The
 map lives in /etc/homelab/svc-hosts/hosts.yml -- edit it and re-run
 homelab-svc-hosts-apply. The block is delimited by BEGIN/END markers and is
 the only part of /etc/hosts this package touches.
 .
 Set `mode: dns` in that file to stop managing /etc/hosts (removing the block)
 once an authoritative svc.homelab DNS zone serves the fleet -- the planned
 convergence from the /etc/hosts seed to real DNS.
